Spec: Semester entity and semester view

Purpose:
  The Semester entity (year and term) and a multi-column vertical list calendar (wall planner) showing one semester
  on one desktop screen. Each month is a column and each day is a row. The view is a read-only aggregation over
  ../courses/courses.sdd, ../realizations/realizations.sdd, ../lessons/lessons.sdd and ../holidays/holidays.sdd.

Owns:
  ./domain.py
  ./ports.py
  ./services.py
  ./repository_sqlite.py
  ./view.py
  ./routes.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Depends on:
  ../shared/shared.sdd
  ../auth/auth.sdd
  ../courses/courses.sdd
  ../realizations/realizations.sdd
  ../lessons/lessons.sdd
  ../holidays/holidays.sdd
  ../no_teach_weeks/no_teach_weeks.sdd
  ../deadlines/deadlines.sdd
  ../conferences/conferences.sdd
  ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd

Must:
  A Semester has a year and a term of `spring` or `fall`; the year and term combination is unique, enforced both
  by @SemesterService and by a unique index on the table.
  Semesters are listed in calendar order: by year, and within a year `spring` before `fall`, since `spring` starts
  the calendar year and `fall` ends it.
  @SemesterService.create_semester rejects any term other than `spring` or `fall` with @InvalidTermError before
  storage, so a crafted request cannot persist a Semester whose period would compute incorrectly.
  @SemesterService.delete_semester removes one Semester, rejecting an unknown id with @UnknownSemesterError; the
  database's foreign keys cascade the deletion to the Semester's CourseRealizations, their Lessons and its
  NoTeachWeeks.
  @SemesterRepository in ./ports.py exposes list, get, add and delete operations backing ./services.py.
  The admin can create a new Semester by submitting a year and a term through a form; the submission is rejected
  by ../auth/auth.sdd's guard for non-admin sessions, and rejected with a validation message when the year+term
  combination already exists.
  Creating a Semester also creates that term's default NoTeachWeeks through ../no_teach_weeks/no_teach_weeks.sdd's
    @NoTeachWeekService, so a new Semester starts with weeks `42` and `51` blocked when its term is `fall`, or weeks
    `1`, `10` and `22` when its term is `spring`, each carrying its own Finnish break title.
  Creating a Semester also pre-populates its dates with Finnish public holidays through
    ../holidays/holidays.sdd's @HolidayService, covering exactly the Semester's period. The two terms of one year
    cover disjoint periods, so no Semester re-populates a date another one already holds.
  When no Semesters exist, ./routes.py renders the create-Semester form as `/`'s primary content for an admin
  session instead of the wall planner; a visitor instead sees a neutral notice and no form. Once at least one
  Semester exists, a small persistent admin-only "+ New Semester" control sits in the header next to the shared
  persistent Semester selector, linking to the same form.
  The semester periods follow a fixed rule from the year and term alone, so any arbitrary Semester's period is
  computed, never looked up: a `fall` Semester spans `<year>-08-01` to `<year>-12-31`; a `spring` Semester spans
  `<year>-01-01` to `<year>-06-30`.
  The container is a CSS grid whose `grid-template-columns` is `repeat(`, one column per month of the selected
  semester, `, 1fr)`, and `gap: 10px`. A semester of five months renders five columns.
  The container height is `100vh` minus the header height and the legend bar's height, so a 1080p screen shows the
  whole semester without vertical or horizontal scrolling. The container itself scrolls in both directions rather
  than clipping, so content that does not fit stays reachable: a viewport too narrow for the columns' minimum widths
  scrolls horizontally, and day rows that no longer fit the container's height scroll vertically.
  The view is laid out for a desktop screen, and a small screen still shows a readable planner rather than a
  crushed one: the weekday abbreviation, the date number and the lesson squares keep their width on a narrow viewport
  and the rest of the semester is reached by scrolling. Complete mobile support is out of scope, so the header and
  the legend bar keep ../shared/shared.sdd's desktop layout.
  Every day row and the month column around it share a minimum width of `8rem`, so no column is narrowed below the
  width its week-number gutter, weekday abbreviation, date number and lesson squares need.
  Each month is a flex column (`display: flex; flex-direction: column`) with the month name as header at its top.
  Each month contains one row per day of that month, and each row has `flex: 1` so all rows share height equally.
  A day row shows the weekday abbreviation, the date number and a wider space for lesson indicators.
  A Monday row shows that Monday's ISO week number in a fixed-width light-grey gutter left of the weekday
  abbreviation, so the number sits in the middle of the Monday that starts the week. No other row shows a number, and
  every row reserves the same gutter, so the weekday labels of a column stay aligned. A week whose Monday falls
  outside the Semester's period has no rendered Monday, so the days before the Semester's own first Monday carry no
  number.
  The day row for today carries a green bar along its left edge; no other day row does.
  Lessons appear as inline-block squares of `12px` by `12px`. The view assigns each CourseRealization a color from a
  fixed palette of ten distinct colors at render time, so a Semester with up to ten CourseRealizations gives each one
  its own color; no color is stored in the database.
  A ../deadlines/deadlines.sdd Deadline appears on its day row as a circle of the same `12px` by `12px`, drawn in the
    color of the CourseRealization it belongs to, the color its Lesson squares share, and at `50%` opacity. Clicking
    a circle navigates to ../realizations/realizations.sdd's weekly view for that Deadline's CourseRealization, the
    same target one of that realization's Lesson squares links to, so an admin's click on a circle opens neither this
    view's day dialog nor any other.
  A day row draws its Lesson squares first and its Deadline circles after them, so a Deadline dated on a day with a
    Lesson overlaps that square instead of pushing it away. A NoTeachWeek's rows suppress the Lesson squares but
    keep the Deadline circles, since a deadline is an obligation rather than teaching.
  A legend bar below the grid names the markers the rows use, for the admin and for a visitor alike: one entry per
  CourseRealization of the shown Semester, in the order the view assigns their colors, each a square in that
  realization's color beside its course name and group, followed by a square labelled as a Lesson and a circle
  labelled as a Deadline. The entries wrap onto further lines instead of scrolling and the bar takes only the height
  it needs, so up to ten CourseRealizations leave the grid fully visible; a Semester with no CourseRealization shows
  the two markers alone.
  Hovering a square shows lesson details through a tooltip that does not change the row height. The tooltip always
  fits the grid area: ../shared/shared.sdd's script opens it above the square when there is room and below it
  otherwise, and keeps it clear of the left-most and right-most month columns, so the first days of a month are
  never cut off by the screen edge or hidden behind the top bar.
  Holidays are visibly distinguished on their day row and show their title.
  A ../conferences/conferences.sdd Conference shows on its day row as purple text beside that day's Holiday or
    NoTeachWeek title, since the two coexist: a date carrying both shows both titles, in their own colors. A day
    holding only a Conference is not tinted, because a Conference blocks nothing, so a tinted row keeps meaning that
    nothing is taught that day.
  Hovering a Conference's purple title shows a tooltip through ../shared/shared.sdd's `data-tip` anchor, as a Lesson
    square does, without changing the row height. The tooltip carries the Conference's own title over the fixed
    sentence `This conference or event might affect teaching schedule or availability of the teacher`.
  A day row holding a Conference opens ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd's Conference tab for the admin, since that is the
    entry the day already has; every other row opens the Lesson tab as before.
  The Monday-to-Friday rows of a NoTeachWeek are distinguished like a Holiday row, with the same tint and the same
  per-row title, and the row shows no lesson squares, since nothing is taught during the week. A Saturday or Sunday
  row keeps the plain weekend tint.
  Saturdays and Sundays are visibly distinguished with the same mild tint as a Holiday row, even on a week with no
  Holiday, since no lessons are taught on weekends by default.
  The wall planner's grid carries the id `semester-grid`, which is the swap target ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd's forms
  post to, so a successful write re-renders this view's own grid rather than a copy of it; ./view.py's @semester_grid
  renders that bare grid without the dialog container for exactly those write responses.
  For the admin, clicking a day row opens the dialog specified in ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd. The wall planner
  renders the dialog's empty container once, and renders day rows with that trigger, a lesson square still links to
  ../realizations/realizations.sdd's weekly view instead of opening the dialog, and a visitor is shown neither.
  Clicking a lesson square navigates to ../realizations/realizations.sdd's weekly view for that lesson's
  CourseRealization.
  ./routes.py registers the view at `/`, reading the Semester to show from the `semester_id` query parameter so a
  link to one Semester's wall planner is shareable; when the parameter is absent or unknown, it defaults to the
  Semester whose period has most recently started on or before today, or the earliest Semester if none has started
  yet. For example, today `2026-10-01` defaults to fall 2026, and a visit on `2027-07-15` (after spring 2027 ends
  and before any later Semester starts) still defaults to spring 2027, the previous one.
  ./routes.py passes every Semester from ./services.py and the shown Semester's id to ../shared/shared.sdd's
  persistent Semester selector, so the admin or visitor can switch Semesters from any tab; switching updates the
  `semester_id` query parameter without a full page reload.

Must not:
  The grid's minimum widths must not widen ../shared/shared.sdd's page shell or make the document itself scroll
  horizontally; the grid stays the only scroll container, so the header and the legend bar never move sideways.

Example:
  semester 1: `2026-08` to `2026-12`
  columns: `repeat(5, 1fr)`
  semester 2: `2027-01` to `2027-06`
  columns: `repeat(6, 1fr)`

Tasks:
  [x] Implement @Semester and the hardcoded academic-year-2026-2027 period rules in ./domain.py, and a hardcoded
    ./services.py (standing in for @SemesterRepository) that returns the single fall-2026 Semester and builds the
    aggregated view-model consumed by ./view.py
  [x] Replace the hardcoded semester lookup in ./services.py with a class-based @SemesterRepository-backed
    `SemesterService` (./ports.py and ./repository_sqlite.py), per ../architecture.sdd's Example
  [x] Render the static month columns and day rows
  [x] Render lesson squares and CSS tooltips through ../realizations/realizations.sdd, ../lessons/lessons.sdd and
    ../courses/courses.sdd services
  [x] Render holidays through ../holidays/holidays.sdd services
  [x] Implement ./routes.py registering the semester view at the `/` route and wire it into ../main.py
  [x] Implement the default-by-date Semester selection in ./domain.py and ./services.py, the Semester dropdown, the
    shareable `semester_id` query parameter, and linking each lesson square to ../realizations/realizations.sdd's
    weekly view
  [x] Make ./domain.py's `default_semester` and `SemesterService.get_default_semester` return `None` instead of
    crashing when no Semesters exist
  [x] Implement ./view.py's create-Semester form and admin-only "+ New Semester" control, and ./routes.py's
    `GET /semesters/new` and `POST /semesters`, gated by ../auth/auth.sdd's guard, rendering the form as `/`'s
    primary content whenever no Semesters exist
  [x] Reject terms other than `spring` or `fall` in @SemesterService.create_semester with @InvalidTermError
  [x] Create the term's default NoTeachWeeks from @SemesterService.create_semester through
    ../no_teach_weeks/no_teach_weeks.sdd, and render a NoTeachWeek's Monday-to-Friday rows as tinted, titled rows
    without lesson squares in ./view.py
  [x] Render the wall planner's grid under the id `semester-grid`, and for an admin render the day-row trigger,
    the link-preserving lesson square and the dialog container that ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd swaps into, passing
    the admin flag from ./routes.py into ./view.py
  [x] Mark the grid as the tooltip area and each lesson square as a tooltip anchor in ./view.py, so a hovered square's
    tooltip opens below the first rows and inside the left-most column instead of leaving the grid
  [x] Add @SemesterService.delete_semester with the matching @SemesterRepository delete operation, relying on the
    database's foreign-key cascade for its CourseRealizations, their Lessons and its NoTeachWeeks
  [x] Pre-populate a new Semester's period with Finnish public holidays from @SemesterService.create_semester through
    ../holidays/holidays.sdd
  [x] Render each ../deadlines/deadlines.sdd Deadline as a half-transparent circle in its realization's own color,
    after that day's lesson squares, in ./view.py, read through @SemesterService in ./services.py
  [x] Link each deadline circle to its realization's weekly view, like that realization's lesson squares
  [x] Extend @PALETTE to ten distinct colors, so a Semester with up to ten CourseRealizations colors each one
    uniquely in ./services.py
  [x] Render each Monday row's ISO week number in a light-grey gutter in ./view.py, read from @DayCell's
    `week_number` built in ./services.py
  [x] Render the legend bar below the grid in ./view.py, listing one entry per CourseRealization in its own color with
    its course name and group plus the Lesson square and Deadline circle markers, and wrap its entries so the bar grows
    downward instead of clipping the grid
  [x] Give every day row and its month column the `8rem` minimum width in ./view.py and let the grid scroll in both
    directions instead of clipping, so the wall planner stays readable on a narrow viewport
  [x] Render each ../conferences/conferences.sdd Conference as purple text with a hover tooltip on its day row, read
    through @ConferenceService in ./services.py, and open the day dialog's Conference tab from a row that holds one

